export anchor DarkTimelineStyle:
    number: 232
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Dark timeline
    idea: The dashboard read as a schedule, where every project is a bar on a shared date axis from October to January with its done share filled, its due date marked and one orange today line cutting through all of them.
    base: dark
    palette:
        ground: #0f1113, the page, fields and the style sheet
        panel: #16191c, the top bar, panels and lanes
        band: #1b1f23, the remaining part of a bar, the current tab and the secondary button
        line: #2a2f35, panel edges, axis rules and the activity spine
        grid: #22272c, weekly grid lines and lane dividers
        ink: #e8eaed, text and the due diamonds
        muted: #9ea6af, labels, dates and axis text
        orange: #ff9f5a, the today line and tag, the date line, the current tab edge, the primary button and focus
        onOrange: #2b1302, text on orange
        done: #86b3ff, the done part of each bar and this week bars
        remaining: #68737f, the bar outline for remaining time
        lastWeek: #6e7884, last week bars
        ok: #7fd69e, the On track word and icon
        risk: #f2c66a, the At risk word and icon
        bad: #ff978a, the Behind word and icon and the overdue line
    type:
        Segoe UI first, then system-ui, Roboto. Dates, axis labels and
        figures in ui-monospace, Cascadia Mono, Menlo, Consolas. Base 14px.
        The greeting is 24px at 650, figures 20px mono at 600, lane names
        14px at 600, dates and axis labels 12px mono, the today tag 11px mono
        at 700.
    layout:
        A 56px panel top bar holds an orange calendar icon with the name, a
        segmented nav with Home raised and edged orange below, search, an
        orange New project button, a square bell and a square MO tile with
        Mara Okafor. Below, the date in orange mono sits over Good morning,
        Mara and a red line reading 4 tasks are overdue, with the four
        figures as one bordered strip on the right. The main panel is
        Project timeline · October to January with a key for done,
        remaining, due date and today. A 250px label column, sticky when the
        panel scrolls, lists each project with category, tasks and status.
        The track area spans 1 October 2026 to 20 January 2027 with month
        labels and weekly grid lines. Each lane draws a bar from a sample
        start date to the due date, outlined for remaining time and filled
        blue for the done share, ends in a diamond with the percent and due
        date, and the orange today line at 31 October crosses every lane
        under a Today 31 Oct tag. Below sit two panels, the daily chart with
        paired weekly bars and the totals in its header, and Recent activity
        as a vertical spine with dots, the newest dot orange. Below 960px
        the nav and search take their own rows and the lower panels stack.
        Below 700px the timeline scrolls sideways inside its panel.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 62px lanes, 16px panel padding, 16px between panels.
    density: Medium. Six lanes on one axis, then chart and activity side by side.
    corners: 4px panels, buttons and fields, 3px bars and the today tag.
    borders: 1px #2a2f35 on panels and the axis, #22272c weekly grid lines. Bars have a 1.5px outline for remaining time.
    shadows: None. The orange today line is the only thing that stands out.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.8 stroke, 16px, and a diamond for each due date.
        Status is a check circle, a triangle or a crossed square with the
        word.
    focus: A 2px orange outline offset 2px, also on the scrolling timeline region.
    tone: Schedule-minded, such as Project timeline, Today 31 Oct, due 20 Nov and Newest first.
